  "answers": [
    "**Weight, October 1\u20132, 2026: 72.57 kg on October 1. No usable reading on October 2.**\n\n- **October 1:** The daily value is the last measurement of the day, taken at 8:00 PM and recorded as 160 lb, which is 72.57 kg. An earlier reading that morning, 72.0 kg, was not used because the daily rule takes only the last reading of each day. Both readings were in valid units, so the difference is only in which one counts.\n- **October 2:** There is no usable value. The one reading that day (158, at 7:00 AM) has no unit recorded, so I excluded it rather than guess whether it was kg or lb. If you know it was pounds, it would be about 71.67 kg. If it was kg, it would be 158 kg, which would be a large jump, so please check the source.\n\nThe average for these two days is 72.57 kg, based on 1 of 2 days with data. The missing day is not counted as zero. The data comes from a Google Takeout import, not a live connection, and the weight trend can't be assessed from only one day."
  ],
